  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aura I  and  II: Onshore wind project in La Guajira</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary objective of the project is the consolidation and development of Greenwood Energy&apos;s wind power portfolio in La Guajira, Colombia (municipalities of Uribia and Maicao), structured into two key stages. The immediate focus is on advancing the Aura Portfolio, a high-development phase consisting of the Aura I and Aura II wind farms (formerly Alpha and Beta) with a combined capacity of 504 MW. This phase spans 388 hectares and features 92 licensed wind turbines, associated infrastructure, and an 80.45 km, 500 kV transmission line; currently, Aura I has completed its detailed engineering, access road, electrical substation, and campsite earthworks, alongside a 41% intervention of its approved area.</narrative>
  </description>
